=== vocabulary ===
A dataset is a kind of dataset.
A source is a kind of storage.
A sink is a kind of storage.
A pipeline run is a kind of process.
A partition is a kind of thing.
A schema is a kind of thing.
A quality check is a kind of thing.
A watermark is a kind of thing.

A dataset has a name, a status, and a row count.
A source has a name, a status, and a uri.
A sink has a name, a status, and a uri.
A pipeline run has a number, a status, a dataset name, and a started at.
A pipeline run can be running or succeeded or failed, called the run status.
A partition has a name, a dataset name, a status, and an updated at.
A schema has a version, a dataset name, and a status.
A quality check has a name, a dataset name, and a status.
A watermark has a dataset name, a value, and an updated at.

Definition: a dataset is stale if its status is "stale".
Definition: a pipeline run is failed if its status is "failed".
Definition: a partition is backfilled if its status is "backfilled".
Definition: a quality check is passing if its status is "passed".
Definition: a watermark is fresh if its updated at is within the last 24 hours.
Definition: a schema is compatible if its status is "compatible".
Definition: a dataset is high volume if its row count exceeds the batch size threshold.
Definition: a dataset is critical if it is stale and it is high volume.

Extraction relates a source to a dataset.
Extraction is read via the extract tool.
Loading relates a dataset to a sink.
Loading is read via the load tool.
Derivation relates a pipeline run to a dataset.
Derivation is read via the transform tool.

The verb to extract (it extracts, it is extracted) means the extraction relation.
The verb to load (it loads, it is loaded) means the loading relation.
The verb to derive (it derives, it is derived) means the derivation relation.

To fetch datasets:
  bind datasets = invoke dataset.list.

To fetch stale datasets:
  bind datasets = invoke dataset.list with status = "stale".

To fetch failed pipeline runs:
  bind pipeline runs = invoke pipeline.list with status = "failed".

To fetch partitions for a dataset:
  bind partitions = invoke partition.list with dataset = the dataset.

To extract a dataset from a source:
  bind dataset = invoke extract with source = the source.

To transform a dataset:
  invoke transform with dataset = the dataset.

To validate the schema for a dataset:
  bind schema = invoke schema.validate with dataset = the dataset.

To load a dataset into a sink:
  invoke load with dataset = the dataset, sink = the sink.

To dedupe records in a dataset:
  invoke record.dedupe with dataset = the dataset.

To backfill a partition:
  invoke partition.backfill with partition = the partition.

To run quality checks on a dataset:
  bind quality check = invoke quality.run with dataset = the dataset.

To read the watermark for a dataset:
  bind watermark = invoke watermark.read with dataset = the dataset.

To replay a pipeline run:
  invoke pipeline.replay with run = the pipeline run.

=== constants ===

The freshness sla is 24 hours.
The batch size threshold is 100000.
The retry budget is 3.

=== instances ===

There is a sink called warehouse sink:
  name = "warehouse"
  status = "active"
  uri = "s3://warehouse/main"

There is a source called object store source:
  name = "object-store"
  status = "active"
  uri = "s3://raw/landing"

=== language ===
Comparison synonyms:
  lags behind = is less than
  exceeds = is more than
  matches = is
Duration synonyms:
  batch window = 4 hours
Assertion synonyms:
  confirm
  ensure

=== tools ===
List Datasets
=============
-- List datasets, optionally by status.
~ dataset.list(status: String) : List

List Pipeline Runs
===================
-- List pipeline runs by status.
~ pipeline.list(status: String) : List

List Partitions
================
-- List partitions for a dataset.
~ partition.list(dataset: Dataset) : List

Extract
=======
-- Extract a dataset from a source.
~ extract(source: Source) : Dataset

Transform
=========
-- Transform a dataset.
~ transform(dataset: Dataset) : Boolean

Validate Schema
===============
-- Validate the schema for a dataset.
~ schema.validate(dataset: Dataset) : Schema

Load
====
-- Load a dataset into a sink.
~ load(dataset: Dataset, sink: Sink) : Boolean

Dedupe Records
==============
-- Dedupe records in a dataset.
~ record.dedupe(dataset: Dataset) : Boolean

Backfill Partition
===================
-- Backfill a partition.
~ partition.backfill(partition: Partition) : Boolean

Run Quality Checks
===================
-- Run quality checks on a dataset.
~ quality.run(dataset: Dataset) : QualityCheck

Read Watermark
==============
-- Read the watermark for a dataset.
~ watermark.read(dataset: Dataset) : Watermark

Replay Pipeline Run
====================
-- Replay a failed pipeline run.
~ pipeline.replay(run: PipelineRun) : Boolean
